  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, and multiprofile+avgpool clearly outperforms both single-profile PCA (0.485) and multiprofile+transformer (0.519). The image modality is very weak (0.208), so RNA encoder quality is the most promising lever. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) in the proven multiprofile+avgpool setting improve accuracy? This is a clean single-variable change from config_002, isolating the encoder effect. Why best use of budget: With 5 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out encoder improvement in the best-known setting is the highest-information experiment. If scvi_n200 helps, it opens a path to test scgpt and multimodal variants with a stronger RNA backbone; if it doesn't, PCA is validated as sufficient and we can pivot to fusion or image-encoder experiments."
